\f1\fs22 \cf3 For payments without association in the \'93References\'94 column, it will go after the paid invoices and the remaining balance of the payment to that supplier\
\cf0\fs24 - In the supplier sheet, if the number of days due is 0, then when creating a new invoice for that supplier, the same as the invoice date will be proposed\
- When creating a new invoice, in the list where I choose the supplier, the first option should be "Add new supplier", which if chosen sends you to the supplier creation screen where it creates a new supplier and after saving it returns to the new invoice creation screen with this newly created supplier already selected\
- When entering the amount, a maximum of 4 decimal places will be accepted after the decimal separator when entering, but saving and displaying will be done by rounding to two\
- in the invoice list, the following display selection criteria have been added to the display selection criteria: - invoice number, - date range, - supplier name\
- in the payment list, the following display selection criteria have been added: - receipt/OP number, - paid invoice number, - date range, - name supplier\
- in the "Manage supplier invoices / payments" screen, a "Due dates" tab has been introduced, which displays due dates divided into 3 categories: overdue, current week and next week\
